<title>USA: San Diego, Calif., $82 mln notes yield 3.95 pct.</title>
<headline>San Diego, Calif., $82 mln notes yield 3.95 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear Stearns &amp; Co said Thursday it priced $82 million San Diego, Calif., tax anticipation notes with a 4.50 percent coupon to yield 3.95 percent.</p>
<p>The notes, which mature on Sept. 30, 1998, are rated SP1-plus by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
